    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T00:08:50Z",
    "body": "Thank you for this clear request, and for the offer to test.\n\nTriage: **P6** (accepted enhancement, not yet scheduled), **effort:high**, **area:post**. A new post changes posted G-code, so it gets the safety-level review. Your option list (retract position, `G43` after a remapped `M6`, `G64 P`, `G33.1` only with a spindle encoder, incremental IJK) is a good spec for it.\n\nClean-room note: CamCraft cannot use Fusion 360 or HSMWorks posts or their output, also not their LinuxCNC posts. We write the post from the LinuxCNC documentation only.\n\nThese help, when you have time:\n- From your INI file: the Z travel limits and the home position (is machine Z0 the top of travel?).\n- What your `M6` remap does: does it apply the tool length offset itself?\n- Does your spindle have an encoder (for `G33.1` rigid tapping)?\n- Later, the sim result and an air cut (spindle off, Z well above the part) of the first posted programs.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
